// Problem Statement

Hercy wants to save money in a bank for n days.

On the first Monday, he deposits $1.

Each following day of the same week, he deposits $1 more than the previous day.

Every new Monday, he deposits $1 more than the previous Monday.

Return the total amount of money deposited after n days.

Approach: Using a Loop

Initialize total = 0 to store the total money.

Initialize monday = 1 for Monday's deposit in the current week.

Loop through all n days.

Add monday + (i % 7) to total, where i % 7 represents the number of days since Monday.

Whenever i % 7 == 6, the week ends, so increase monday by 1.

Return total.//







class Solution {
    public int totalMoney(int n) {
        int total = 0;
        int monday = 1;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            total += monday + (i % 7);
            
            if (i % 7 == 6) {
                monday++;
            }
        }

        return total;
    }
}
